                    Travel Hike & Eat (“THE”) is entering an important transition from a founder-led travel and social community into a professionally operated, revenue-generating travel, experiences, and lifestyle business.



The Executive Assistant & Operations Coordinator will work directly with THE’s Founder/CEO and will be responsible for creating leverage around the CEO’s time, priorities, communications, projects, travel, vendors, and growing operating calendar.  The position reports directly to the Founder/CEO and is a hybrid in office/VA position.



This is not intended to be a traditional clerical assistant or basic virtual-assistant position. THE is looking for someone who can combine strong executive-assistant fundamentals with project coordination, organization, judgment, follow-through, research, and operational ownership.



The successful candidate should become the person who helps ensure that:



priorities do not fall through the cracks;

decisions and follow-ups are documented;

vendors and contractors remain accountable;

meetings produce clear actions;

travel and event logistics are organized;

the CEO receives concise information needed to make decisions; and

recurring administrative work increasingly operates without requiring the CEO's direct involvement.



The position will work closely with THE’s Digital Operations/Website Manager, outside website and marketing agencies, tour operators, vendors, assistant organizers, and future employees and contractors.



Strong candidates will likely possess approximately four or more years of meaningful executive-assistant, operations, project-coordination, chief-of-staff support, or similar experience.



Exceptional candidates with somewhat different backgrounds may also be considered.



Required Capabilities



Candidates should demonstrate:



exceptional written and spoken English;

professional communication;

strong organizational ability;

project-management discipline;

excellent follow-through;

mature judgment;

confidentiality;

strong attention to detail;

comfort working independently;

ability to prioritize conflicting demands;

comfort working directly with a founder/CEO;

ability to learn unfamiliar subjects quickly;

confidence communicating with senior professionals and vendors.
